About LLM licensing

This repository uses separate licenses for software and documentation.

1. Software: MIT

Source code, executable examples, tests, configuration, CI definitions,
stylesheets, JavaScript, and templates are licensed under the MIT License in
LICENSE-CODE. This includes code under src/, scripts/, tests/, projects/,
docs/javascripts/, docs/stylesheets/, and docs/overrides/.

2. Documentation: CC BY 4.0

Prose, diagrams, and other instructional content are licensed under the
Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License described in
LICENSE-DOCS. This includes Markdown documentation in docs/, README files,
CONTRIBUTING.md, and CHANGELOG.md.

3. Mixed files and third-party material

In Jupyter notebooks, code cells use the MIT License and Markdown cells use
CC BY 4.0. When a file contains both software and prose, each portion follows
the corresponding rule above. A file-specific notice overrides this routing.
Third-party dependencies, models, datasets, images, quotations, and other
materials remain subject to their own licenses and terms.
